    {
      "external_key": "q-calculus-1-limits-continuity",
      "topic": "Limits",
      "subtopic": "Continuity",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "kind": "template",
      "statement": "For what value of $k$ is $f(x) = \\begin{cases} {{coef(a,'x')}} {{signed(b)}} & x < {{c}} \\\\ x^2 + k & x \\ge {{c}} \\end{cases}$ continuous at $x = {{c}}$? (Here $k$ is the unknown.)",
      "answer": "$k = {{a*c + b - c*c}}$",
      "solution": "Continuity needs the two pieces to agree at $x = {{c}}$. The left piece gives ${{a}}({{c}}) {{signed(b)}} = {{a*c + b}}$; the right gives $({{c}})^2 + k = {{c*c}} + k$. Setting them equal, $k = {{a*c + b}} - {{c*c}} = {{a*c + b - c*c}}$.",
      "tags": [
        "limits",
        "functions"
      ],
